\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Training curves.} Reward of the current (unperturbed) policy on each iteration's 6 training objects. Both methods improve on the model controller (dotted) within about 600 episodes. The unshielded runs dip whenever an iteration's batch contains a lift that slips: three of the five B2 runs ended on such a batch. The shielded runs never fail and converge to the same reward, about $-0.50$.}}{20}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
